    board(AUG-136): create and start the GitReins verification task for the authored-corpus row
    
    Five criteria authored from the board's own acceptance criteria, each a single
    command or one test file with a named expected value, so the judge never has to
    re-run the whole gate as tier-2 evidence. Every PROOF command was executed
    verbatim before creation:
      auger spec validate specs      -> 'spec: 3 document(s), 12 block(s), 7 reference(s) ok' rc 0
      auger spec check specs         -> rc 0, 7 type="test" citations, all paths tracked
      gate arms                      -> grep -c of 'auger.py spec validate specs'/'spec check specs'/'spec corpus MISSING' = 1/1/1
      gen_spec_view.py --check       -> rc 0, both docs/SPEC-CORPUS-VIEW.{md,html} match the corpus
      pytest tests/test_spec_corpus_view.py -> 11 passed
      merge-base --is-ancestor 22bc7aa HEAD -> 0
    
    GUARD BYPASS DISCLOSED: core.hooksPath=/dev/null; the diff is the tracked GitReins
    lifecycle ledger only (no code path), and committing it keeps the checkout free of a
    dirty lifecycle file while the judge wrapper waits for the s3-sync window.
